cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If this repository helps you, you may cite it as below. It is an informal
  synthesis of published research, written with Claude, an AI assistant by
  Anthropic. It is not an official standard, not peer-reviewed, and not a new
  result.
title: "reader-ergonomics-learning"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-29"
abstract: >-
  How to write material meant to be learned (a lesson, worked examples, an
  exercise sheet, a study guide, flashcards, and the questions inside them) so
  that someone who studies it alone retains it and uses it on new problems. It
  extends reader-ergonomics and derives its shapes from reader-ergonomics-topic.
  Four audited multivocal literature reviews (420 sources) support five shapes
  of study documents, with checks a program runs on them.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Tewf"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tewf/reader-ergonomics-learning"
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - learning materials
  - instructional design
  - retrieval practice
  - flashcards
  - worked examples
  - literature review
